{"title":"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_30\">Problem 30</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 30\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many distinct ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy the following equations?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0dc897d6b7f792bf621566502c97fc28f8b9d4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x + 2y + 4z &amp;= 12 \\\\ xy + 4yz + 2xz &amp;= 22 \\\\ xyz &amp;= 6 \\end{align*}\" width=\"162\" height=\"65\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c678ec9fc880c5a8741b33f073f6ce288dc5136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\text{none}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }4\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"378\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first equation suggests the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e6ffafd895479ec914509705172f3db4237ab55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)=(x,2y,4z),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"20\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/037c5bc0742492bb1c05d28316f6404cdae2d48e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)=\\left(a,\\frac b2,\\frac c4\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"172\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>We rewrite the given equations in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d81ffe14dc65d342d075662e3f3bd00898dbd2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c:$\" width=\"16\" height=\"8\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/66811a666758c34ab7814675e8749cd28183469c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a + b + c &amp;= 12, \\\\ \\frac{ab}{2} + \\frac{bc}{2} + \\frac{ac}{2} &amp;= 22, \\\\ \\frac{abc}{8} &amp;= 6. \\end{align*}\" width=\"151\" height=\"106\" />\nWe clear fractions in these equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/980dae7f19cd0407cc84504e2a9ab8ba91040bb8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a + b + c &amp;= 12, \\\\ ab + ac + bc &amp;= 44, \\\\ abc &amp;= 48. \\end{align*}\" width=\"141\" height=\"63\" />\nBy Vieta's formulas, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the roots of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e36a8916d916bc7e812e7f2bb0f517ec10a3e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^3 - 12r^2 + 44r - 48 = 0,\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"19\" />\nwhich factors as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be36feadab3cb3db097c54ae5002a634e26e7b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(r - 2)(r - 4)(r - 6) = 0.\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/151aaaedb2053eff0effb211db6e734cf424d6fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a,b,c\\}=\\{2,4,6\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" /> For each permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf453512ebf161171f4b07f597c63281cbf607b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" /> we find the corresponding ordered triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/1515bf2dc29f19c51dfee8a763f9a6623e79a870.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)=\\left(a,\\frac b2,\\frac c4\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"172\" height=\"45\" /> as shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc1a84e76c2c726cc95293f256b652fcfd077f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c||c|c|c} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2.5ex] \\boldsymbol{a} &amp; \\boldsymbol{b} &amp; \\boldsymbol{c} &amp; \\boldsymbol{x} &amp; \\boldsymbol{y} &amp; \\boldsymbol{z} \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] 2 &amp; 4 &amp; 6 &amp; 2 &amp; 2 &amp; 3/2 \\\\ 2 &amp; 6 &amp; 4 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 1 \\\\ 4 &amp; 2 &amp; 6 &amp; 4 &amp; 1 &amp; 3/2 \\\\ 4 &amp; 6 &amp; 2 &amp; 4 &amp; 3 &amp; 1/2 \\\\ 6 &amp; 2 &amp; 4 &amp; 6 &amp; 1 &amp; 1 \\\\ 6 &amp; 4 &amp; 2 &amp; 6 &amp; 2 &amp; 1/2 \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"151\" />\nSo, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107d22cf8cea8e2bc3744cf7bdac7cdfd2af688c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" /> such ordered triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2193c436d7ec14c9b8f228ac28879d63c64b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (credit given to AoPS)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME\" title=\"1976 AHSME\">1976 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1976 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1976\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wik